{{!
    @template local_pshub/course_card

    One course, on the home page or in the catalogue.

    The context comes from catalogue_service::present(), which resolves price
    and badges through price_resolver - the same resolver the paywall uses, so
    a card can never advertise a figure the checkout disagrees with. The price
    arrives preformatted: templates do no arithmetic, and none of them needs to
    know that XAF has no subunit.

    A card shows the course's own image when one has been uploaded, and the
    language on a brand ground when none has. The plate is not a placeholder to
    be replaced later - it is what keeps a catalogue scannable and a new course
    publishable on the day it is written, with no photograph and nothing to
    download.

    The whole card is ONE link. A card with a link inside it is a card most of
    whose surface does nothing, which on a phone is the difference between one
    tap and three.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * url - Course detail page.
    * fullname - Course name.
    * langplate - Language code, uppercase, shown on the coloured ground.
    * cardtone - 1-4, which ground this course gets.
    * cefr_level, session_duration_minutes, is_one_to_one - the meta line.
    * isfree, hasdiscount, priceformatted, pricebaseformatted - price.
    * topbadge - {label, style}, or absent when the course carries no type.
    * hideprice - True in the learner's own space, where the course is already
      theirs and the price is noise rather than information.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": "/local/pshub/course.php?id=4",
        "fullname": "Anglais général — A2",
        "langplate": "EN",
        "cardtone": 2,
        "cefr_level": "A2",
        "session_duration_minutes": 50,
        "is_one_to_one": false,
        "isfree": false,
        "hasdiscount": true,
        "priceformatted": "20 000 FCFA",
        "pricebaseformatted": "25 000 FCFA",
        "topbadge": {"label": "-20 %", "style": "promo"}
    }
}}
<article class="ps-card ps-card--tone{{cardtone}}">
    <a class="ps-card__link" href="{{url}}">

        <span class="ps-card__plate">
            {{#hasimage}}
                {{!
                    alt is empty on purpose: the course title sits directly
                    under this image and says the same thing. A screen reader
                    announcing both would read every card twice.

                    Lazy and async because a catalogue is a grid of these, and
                    on a 2G connection the ones below the fold must not compete
                    with the ones on it (§13.2).
                }}
                <img class="ps-card__image" src="{{imageurl}}" alt=""
                     loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            {{/hasimage}}
            {{^hasimage}}
                <span class="ps-card__plate-text">{{langplate}}</span>
            {{/hasimage}}
            {{#topbadge}}
                <span class="ps-badge ps-badge--{{style}}">{{label}}</span>
            {{/topbadge}}
        </span>

        <span class="ps-card__body">
            <span class="ps-card__title">{{fullname}}</span>

            <span class="ps-card__meta">
                {{#cefr_level}}{{cefr_level}} · {{/cefr_level}}
                {{#str}}card_duration, local_pshub, {{session_duration_minutes}}{{/str}}
                {{#is_one_to_one}} · {{#str}}card_onetoone, local_pshub{{/str}}{{/is_one_to_one}}
            </span>

            {{^hideprice}}
            <span class="ps-card__price">
                {{#isfree}}
                    <span class="ps-price-now ps-price-now--free">{{#str}}card_free, local_pshub{{/str}}</span>
                {{/isfree}}
                {{^isfree}}
                    {{#hasdiscount}}<span class="ps-price-was">{{pricebaseformatted}}</span>{{/hasdiscount}}
                    <span class="ps-price-now">{{priceformatted}}</span>
                {{/isfree}}
            </span>
            {{/hideprice}}

            {{!
                The action depends on where the card is. In the catalogue it
                invites someone to look at a course; in the learner's own space
                the course is already theirs, so it opens.
            }}
            <span class="ps-card__cta">
                {{#ctalabel}}{{ctalabel}}{{/ctalabel}}
                {{^ctalabel}}{{#str}}card_view, local_pshub{{/str}}{{/ctalabel}}
            </span>
        </span>

    </a>
</article>
